From 47143643f781db9ec88d988d9a47a61f83b57f79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:19:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: CN7 non-SCC steer ramp 3 -> 4/frame, STEER_MAX
 unchanged (384)

Logged EPS output (MDPS12 CR_Mdps_OutTq) saturates near a ~270-300 LKAS11 command on this car, so a higher
STEER_MAX buys ~nothing; the measurable loss in sharp low-speed turns is the 3/frame ramp. 4 is the largest
rate the panda real-time check (112 per 250 ms) admits for a continuous ramp.

Rebased onto the current series-applied tip (fca11-long, patch 0014): the SP param bit moves 256 -> 1024 because
0014 shipped HYUNDAI_PARAM_SP_FCA11_LONG = 256; 512 stays reserved for steer-test's unshipped LKAS_PARK_TEST so
both can coexist. Diff semantics are otherwise identical to the original preparation.

- CarControllerParams: STEER_DELTA_UP = 4 for HYUNDAI_ELANTRA_2022_NON_SCC only
- interface: sets HyundaiSafetyFlagsSP.CN7_STEER_RAMP (1024) for that platform only
- panda: HYUNDAI_STEERING_LIMITS_CN7_RAMP = HYUNDAI_LIMITS(384, 4, 7), honored only with NON_SCC and
  never over ALT_LIMITS / ALT_LIMITS_2
- tests: full inherited torque suite at rate-up 4, boundary/gating tests, car-layer gating + C/Python mirror
